Lumen 0.0.4 (01 Nov 2026) - test build
=====================================

A photo library and editor for RISC OS 5, in the spirit of Aperture.
This test build has importing, browsing, rating, flagging and albums;
adjustments (white balance with an eyedropper, exposure, levels,
contrast, saturation, vibrancy); Auto; crop, quarter turns, straighten
and perspective; grids; presets; and copying adjustments between photos.
Your photos are never changed: each edit is a recipe kept in the
library, and can be undone or reset at any time.

Getting started
---------------
Double-click !Lumen. Its library window opens. Drag a folder of photos
(JPEG or PNG) from the Filer onto the window or the icon bar icon. Lumen
reads them in the background and makes thumbnails; the desktop stays
usable while it works. Your photos are never changed or moved: the
library only refers to them.

The library lives in <Choices$Write>.Lumen.Library (normally inside
!Boot.Choices). To keep it elsewhere, set Lumen$Library before running
!Lumen, e.g.  *Set Lumen$Library SDFS::RISCOSpi.$.Photos.Library

Keys (with the library window focused)
--------------------------------------
  0 to 5        set the rating of the selected photos
  9             reject (rejected photos leave All photos)
  /             flag or unflag
  Cursor keys   move to the next photo; Page Up/Down, Home, End too
  Ctrl-A        select all
  Escape        clear the selection
  Ctrl-C        copy the adjustments of the (first) selected photo
  Ctrl-V        paste them onto the selected photos

  Return        open the focused photo in the viewer (or double-click)

The viewer
----------
The photo on the left, the adjustments on the right. Drag a slider: the
photo follows (at half resolution while you drag, then in full). Click
Adjust on a slider to put it back to its default; "Reset" beside a group
resets the group. Every change is saved as you make it.

The tools above the sliders:
  Auto          sets white balance, exposure, levels, contrast and
                vibrancy from the photo itself (one undo step; it leaves
                any crop or straightening alone)
  Crop          shows the whole photo with the crop over it. Drag a
                corner or an edge, drag inside to move it, or drag
                outside to draw a new one. Return (or Done) crops, Escape
                puts the old crop back. Photo > Crop shape fixes the
                shape: Original, Square, 3:2, 4:3, 16:9 (it follows the
                crop's way round, so a tall crop is 2:3)
  Grid          None, Thirds, Quarters, Fine; while you straighten, a
                fine grid shows anyway
  Presets       apply a saved look, save the current one by name, or
                delete one. A preset keeps the look, not the crop

White Balance: "Pick" then click something that should be grey or white
(a cloud, a wall, a shirt); "Auto" works it out from the whole photo.
Geometry: -90 and +90 turn the photo; Straighten (up to 15 degrees
either way), Vertical and Horizontal (perspective) zoom in just enough
that no empty corners show.

  Left, Right   previous and next photo
  A             Auto
  C             crop (Return to crop, Escape to cancel)
  [ ]           turn 90 degrees anticlockwise, clockwise
  G             next grid
  W             pick white balance
  M             before and after (the original, and back)
  Ctrl-Z        undo          Ctrl-Y   redo
  Ctrl-C        copy the adjustments   Ctrl-V   paste them here
  0 to 5, 9, /  rating, reject, flag, as in the library
  Escape, V     back to the library
  Menu          all of the above, plus Crop shape, Grid and Presets

Edited photos are marked "Edited" in the library, and their thumbnails
are made again with the edit.

Speed: !Lumen.Bench measures the editing pipeline on your machine. Run it
in a task window (Ctrl-F12):  *Run <Lumen$Dir>.Bench

Mouse
-----
  Select        select a photo (click on space to clear)
  Adjust        add a photo to the selection or take it out
  Menu          the Lumen menu

The Lumen menu
--------------
  Show            All photos, Flagged, Rejected, Last import, a project
                  (one per imported folder), an album, or a rating filter
  Selection       rating, flag, reject, select all, clear, copy and
                  paste adjustments, apply a preset
  Album           make a new album from the selection, add to one,
                  or remove from the album shown
  Thumbnail size  Small, Medium, Large

Needs
-----
RISC OS 5.30 or later on a Raspberry Pi 4, 400 or CM4 (other ARMv7
machines should work), and the SharedUnixLibrary 1.16+ and ARMEABISupport
modules from PackMan.

